What is iloc?

iloc stands for Integer Location.

It is used to select rows and columns using integer positions (index numbers).

Example
import pandas as pd

data = {
    "Name": ["Arun", "Priya", "Ravi", "Kiran"],
    "Age": [20, 19, 21, 22],
    "Marks": [85, 92, 78, 88]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)

print(df.iloc[0])      # First row
print(df.iloc[2])      # Third row
print(df.iloc[1:3])    # Second and third rows





         #loc
It is used to select rows and columns using row labels (index labels).

Example
print(df.loc[0])    # First row
print(df.loc[2])    # Third row
print(df.loc[0:2]    #it will print 0,1,2 rows.but when you use iloc it will print correctly 0 and  1st rows

When the DataFrame uses the default index (0, 1, 2...), loc and iloc may produce the same result.    



